# Testing

## Commands

```bash
npm test                 # run the full suite once (Vitest)
npx vitest               # watch mode
```

## When you MUST add or extend tests (same change, not later)

- Adding or changing a parser, validator, or normalizer in `apps/scraper`
- Adding or changing pure functions in `packages/`
- Fixing a bug that could regress — add the test that would have FAILED before the fix
- Supporting a new patch-notes era/layout — add a fixture for it

## When tests are optional

- Config or env-only changes (still run the existing suite before committing)
- Documentation and copy changes

## Fixture rules

- Parser/normalizer tests run against committed HTML fixtures in `apps/scraper/fixtures/` — NEVER the network. Tests must pass offline.
- Fixtures are real downloaded pages; keep at least one per distinct page layout era (currently: 2.6a, 5.0, 7.2b patches, champions list, champion detail, patch index).
- Assert concrete known values (e.g. Jayce Base Armor 46 → 37 in patch 7.2b), not just "no throw".

## Layout

```
apps/scraper/test/*.test.ts      # tests
apps/scraper/fixtures/*.html     # committed page snapshots
```

Database write paths (packages/database) are exercised by running the scraper jobs against a dev database, not by unit tests, until an integration harness exists.
